format writes every line back with a bare LF, so a CRLF document loses every
CR it had. The runner says so in words above the diff.

What it should do: notice the line ending the document already uses and write
the output with that ending.

Cause: BlockFormatter builds its output by appending "\n" literally, in every
one of its cases, and FormatCommand hands that straight to stdout. Nothing
anywhere records what the source used. A fix has to detect the dominant ending
when the source is read and re-apply it on the way out.

Why it matters: formatting a file written on Windows rewrites every line of
it. One tidy-up turns into a whole-file diff, and every line of the real
change is buried in it.
